cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FamilyForge, please cite it as below."
title: "FamilyForge: pedigree-aware Mendelian and ACMG-style interpretation of a family callset (VCF + pedigree + panel -> ranked candidates + reports)"
abstract: >-
  FamilyForge is a disease-agnostic, pure-Python clinical variant-interpretation tool
  that takes a multi-sample annotated VCF, a PED pedigree, and a gene panel for one
  family and produces segregation-checked candidate variants under Mendelian inheritance
  models (de novo/dominant, autosomal-recessive homozygous, compound heterozygous, and
  X-linked recessive), pragmatic ACMG-style A/B/C tiering, a CNV deletion cross-check,
  genotype-based relatedness/sex QC, and audience-specific clinician, publication, and
  letterhead clinical reports. It is the interpretation counterpart to the CallForge
  analysis pipeline and consumes its annotated joint callset (and optional cnv_calls.tsv
  and provenance.json).
authors:
